01:01:45,818 --> 01:01:48,095
- Where be your gibes now?

1483
01:01:48,095 --> 01:01:49,214
Your gambols.

1484
01:01:49,214 --> 01:01:50,858
- [Servo] So they banned you from jesting.

1485
01:01:50,858 --> 01:01:54,599
- Your songs, your flashes
of merriment that were

1486
01:01:54,599 --> 01:01:57,266
wont to set the table on a roar?

1487
01:01:58,762 --> 01:02:01,801
Not one, now, to mock your own grinning?

1488
01:02:01,801 --> 01:02:03,723
- [Mike] Well there was
that one now that mocked.

1489
01:02:03,723 --> 01:02:05,390
- Quite chop-fallen?

1490
01:02:07,398 --> 01:02:11,481
- Now get you to my lady’s
chamber, and tell her:

1491
01:02:13,005 --> 01:02:17,172
let her paint an inch thick,
to this favour she must come!

1492
01:02:18,860 --> 01:02:20,777
Make her laugh at that.

1493
01:02:22,073 --> 01:02:23,480
- [Crow] Please speak
up, my tympanic membrane

1494
01:02:23,480 --> 01:02:25,148
rotted away some years ago.

1495
01:02:25,148 --> 01:02:27,565
- Horatio, tell me one thing.

1496
01:02:28,435 --> 01:02:30,830
Dost thou think Alexander
looked o’ this fashion,

1497
01:02:30,830 --> 01:02:32,048
i’ the earth?

1498
01:02:32,048 --> 01:02:34,452
- [Servo] I don't know,
man, let's go to the tavern.

1499
01:02:34,452 --> 01:02:35,285
- E'en so.

1500
01:02:36,655 --> 01:02:37,818
- And smelt so?

1501
01:02:37,818 --> 01:02:39,735
- [Mike] Oh it did too.

1502
01:02:40,938 --> 01:02:43,000
- [Crow] Ah forget it, I never knew him.

1503
01:02:43,000 --> 01:02:45,039
I made it all up.

1504
01:02:45,039 --> 01:02:47,900
- To what base uses we
may return, Horatio!

1505
01:02:47,900 --> 01:02:50,440
- [Servo] God, that's not dirt!

1506
01:02:50,440 --> 01:02:52,655
- Why, may not imagination
trace the noble dust

1507
01:02:52,655 --> 01:02:55,956
of Alexander till it be
found stopping a bung-hole.

1508
01:02:55,956 --> 01:02:57,123
- [Mike] Dude.

1509
01:02:58,172 --> 01:03:01,081
- ’Twere to consider too
curiously to consider so.

1510
01:03:01,081 --> 01:03:01,914
- No, no.

1511
01:03:03,676 --> 01:03:06,252
Alexander died, Alexander was buried,

1512
01:03:06,252 --> 01:03:10,387
Alexander returneth to
dust, the dust is earth,

1513
01:03:10,387 --> 01:03:13,580
of earth we make loam and why of that loam

1514
01:03:13,580 --> 01:03:17,734
whereto he was converted might
they not stop a beer-barrel?

1515
01:03:17,734 --> 01:03:20,091
- [Crow] It's the ice cream man!

1516
01:03:20,091 --> 01:03:21,846
(bell tolling)

1517
01:03:21,846 --> 01:03:23,990
- [Servo] Here comes
my cow, I've got to go.

1518
01:03:23,990 --> 01:03:26,573
(bell tolling)

1519
01:03:40,180 --> 01:03:43,696
- Hello and welcome to I'll ask for who?

1520
01:03:43,696 --> 01:03:45,935
Now as you know, last
week our reigning champion

1521
01:03:45,935 --> 01:03:49,786
Mr. Tom Servo won the
four-week supply of mutton.

1522
01:03:49,786 --> 01:03:52,406
And he's back this week to
face another challenger.

1523
01:03:52,406 --> 01:03:53,772
(applause)

1524
01:03:53,772 --> 01:03:55,107
- Thanks, Mike, thanks.

1525
01:03:55,107 --> 01:03:56,452
- Tom, remind the folks at home

1526
01:03:56,452 --> 01:03:57,544
what you're doing here.

1527
01:03:57,544 --> 01:04:00,633
- Mike I am a small
robot who lives with you.

1528
01:04:00,633 --> 01:04:02,097
- Robot who lives with me.

1529
01:04:02,097 --> 01:04:03,806
That's interesting, okay
and your challenger,

1530
01:04:03,806 --> 01:04:04,973
Crow T. Robot.

1531
01:04:05,850 --> 01:04:06,755
How are you, sir?

1532
01:04:06,755 --> 01:04:08,318
- I'm feeling good, Mike, thanks.

1533
01:04:08,318 --> 01:04:09,653
- And what do you do, sir?

1534
01:04:09,653 --> 01:04:12,844
- I am also a small
robot who lives with you.

1535
01:04:12,844 --> 01:04:15,102
- Wow, seems to be a
popular job these days.

1536
01:04:15,102 --> 01:04:16,503
(laughing)

1537
01:04:16,503 --> 01:04:17,753
- It really is.

1538
01:04:19,012 --> 01:04:19,942
- Let's get down to action.

1539
01:04:19,942 --> 01:04:21,665
Okay for you folks at home, the object

1540
01:04:21,665 --> 01:04:24,220
of the game is to visually identify a

1541
01:04:24,220 --> 01:04:28,588
person by some part of his
or her skeletal system.

1542
01:04:28,588 --> 01:04:33,079
And, Servo, you'll be starting
with this lovely femur.

1543
01:04:33,079 --> 01:04:33,964
- Ooh.

1544
01:04:33,964 --> 01:04:34,797
- Okay.

1545
01:04:34,797 --> 01:04:35,745
- You have 10 seconds, go.

1546
01:04:35,745 --> 01:04:37,943
- Let's see, I'll ask for Larry Hagman.

1547
01:04:37,943 --> 01:04:41,249
No, no, I'll ask for Katherine Graham.

1548
01:04:41,249 --> 01:04:42,679
No.

1549
01:04:42,679 --> 01:04:45,596
I got it, I'll ask for Biz Markie.

1550
01:04:45,596 --> 01:04:47,151
- Exactly.

1551
01:04:47,151 --> 01:04:49,545
Biz Markie, this is his femur.

1552
01:04:49,545 --> 01:04:50,804
(applause)

1553
01:04:50,804 --> 01:04:52,065
Surprisingly delicate, isn't it?

1554
01:04:52,065 --> 01:04:53,155
All right, well played.

1555
01:04:53,155 --> 01:04:54,232
Now, Crow, ready to give it a whirl?

1556
01:04:54,232 --> 01:04:55,464
- Oh I sure am, Mike.

1557
01:04:55,464 --> 01:04:59,131
- Okay then, here's a
clavicle, who's is it?

1558
01:05:00,849 --> 01:05:02,840
- Wow, I want to say Tim Conway.

1559
01:05:02,840 --> 01:05:05,421
But no, more like Dr. Dean Ornish.

1560
01:05:05,421 --> 01:05:08,226
Germaine Greer, Peter Cetera.

1561
01:05:08,226 --> 01:05:09,415
Jeez no, no, no.

1562
01:05:09,415 --> 01:05:11,671
I'm going to go with Nancy Allen, Mike.

1563
01:05:11,671 --> 01:05:13,648
- Please state it in, I'll ask for form.

1564
01:05:13,648 --> 01:05:16,513
- Oh yeah, I'll ask for Nancy Allen.

1565
01:05:16,513 --> 01:05:17,554
- Is right.

1566
01:05:17,554 --> 01:05:19,002
(bell dinging)

1567
01:05:19,002 --> 01:05:20,748
That's a fine clavicle here.

1568
01:05:20,748 --> 01:05:22,532
Must have drank lots of milk.

1569
01:05:22,532 --> 01:05:24,587
(laughing)

1570
01:05:24,587 --> 01:05:26,012
Okay it's all tied up.

1571
01:05:26,012 --> 01:05:28,762
Cervo, who belongs to this ilium?

1572
01:05:30,575 --> 01:05:31,421
- Oh that's easy, Mike.

1573
01:05:31,421 --> 01:05:34,290
I'll ask for Alaska senator Ted Stevens.

1574
01:05:34,290 --> 01:05:37,496
Wait no, I'm sorry, I'll
ask for Roland Gift.

1575
01:05:37,496 --> 01:05:39,410
Yeah, yeah, I'm going
to go with I'll ask for

1576
01:05:39,410 --> 01:05:41,109
Roland Gift.

1577
01:05:41,109 --> 01:05:45,249
- Ooh, no, I'm sorry I'll
ask for Alaska senator

1578
01:05:45,249 --> 01:05:46,626
Ted Stevens.

1579
01:05:46,626 --> 01:05:47,641
- Oh darn.

1580
01:05:47,641 --> 01:05:48,554
(laughing)

1581
01:05:48,554 --> 01:05:49,513
- Close though, okay.

1582
01:05:49,513 --> 01:05:51,488
Now you could win this one.

1583
01:05:51,488 --> 01:05:52,321
- Wow.

1584
01:05:52,321 --> 01:05:55,904
- Who are these series
of metatarsal bones?

1585
01:05:57,218 --> 01:05:59,096
- Oh I know this one, easy.

1586
01:05:59,096 --> 01:06:00,839
Ralph Waite.

1587
01:06:00,839 --> 01:06:04,657
- They are indeed the
metatarsals of Ralph Waite.

1588
01:06:04,657 --> 01:06:06,781
But alas, incorrect
form for the second time

1589
01:06:06,781 --> 01:06:08,403
and so you don't get the point.

1590
01:06:08,403 --> 01:06:10,443
So nobody wins and you both lose,

1591
01:06:10,443 --> 01:06:12,077
and that's all the time we have.

1592
01:06:12,077 --> 01:06:13,362
(laughing)

1593
01:06:13,362 --> 01:06:14,789
We'll be back next week
with another edition

1594
01:06:14,789 --> 01:06:16,373
of I'll Ask For Who?

1595
01:06:16,373 --> 01:06:18,442
(applause)

1596
01:06:18,442 --> 01:06:21,216
- Mike we won't really be
back next week, will we?

1597
01:06:21,216 --> 01:06:23,135
- Not unless I get a cod piece.

1598
01:06:23,135 --> 01:06:24,721
(applause)

1599
01:06:24,721 --> 01:06:27,304
(upbeat music)

1600
01:06:30,946 --> 01:06:33,857
(bell tolling)

1601
01:06:33,857 --> 01:06:37,169
Ah, the Saint Olaf's Day parade
is pretty dour this year.

1602
01:06:37,169 --> 01:06:39,752
(bell tolling)

1603
01:06:40,599 --> 01:06:41,721
- [Servo] Hey, kid, you
want to speed it up?

1604
01:06:41,721 --> 01:06:43,805
We got three of these today.

1605
01:06:43,805 --> 01:06:46,388
(bell tolling)

1606
01:06:49,476 --> 01:06:51,730
- [Mike] Can barely keep my head cake on.

1607
01:06:51,730 --> 01:06:54,313
(bell tolling)

1608
01:06:57,470 --> 01:06:59,042
- What ceremony else?

1609
01:06:59,042 --> 01:07:00,813
- [Crow] Shut up.

1610
01:07:00,813 --> 01:07:02,426
- Her obsequies have been as far enlarged

1611
01:07:02,426 --> 01:07:06,428
as we have warrant,
her death was doubtful.

1612
01:07:06,428 --> 01:07:09,997
- [Servo] Shouldn't we check then?

1613
01:07:09,997 --> 01:07:12,796
- I'll say no more be done.

1614
01:07:12,796 --> 01:07:13,629
- No more.

1615
01:07:15,094 --> 01:07:18,120
- [Servo] Gee your tunic smells terrific.

1616
01:07:18,120 --> 01:07:19,769
With the legs, we do not have time to take

1617
01:07:19,769 --> 01:07:22,168
a beef-eater to the hospital.

1618
01:07:22,168 --> 01:07:24,751
(bell tolling)

1619
01:07:25,734 --> 01:07:29,379
- [Crow] Oh, man, I was
invited to this, I forgot.

1620
01:07:29,379 --> 01:07:30,553
- Farwell.

1621
01:07:30,553 --> 01:07:32,921
- [Mike] That's really
an all-purpose dress.

1622
01:07:32,921 --> 01:07:36,533
- I hoped thou shouldst
have been my Hamlet’s wife;

1623
01:07:36,533 --> 01:07:39,208
I thought thy bride-bed to have decked,

1624
01:07:39,208 --> 01:07:43,355
sweet maid, and not to
have strewed thy grave!

1625
01:07:43,355 --> 01:07:44,489
- Ophelia.

1626
01:07:44,489 --> 01:07:48,211
- [Crow] I wonder what her skull is like.

1627
01:07:48,211 --> 01:07:49,932
- Hold off the earth a while.

1628
01:07:49,932 --> 01:07:54,372
- [Servo] Stop the
world, I want to get off.

1629
01:07:54,372 --> 01:07:56,219
Even in death, he just goes in her room.

1630
01:07:56,219 --> 01:07:59,419
- Now pile your dust
upon the quick and dead,

1631
01:07:59,419 --> 01:08:04,331
till of this flat a mountain
you have made to o’ertop

1632
01:08:04,331 --> 01:08:07,998
old Ossa or the skyish
head of blue Olympus.

1633
01:08:09,414 --> 01:08:13,207
- Who is he whose grief
bears such an emphasis?

1634
01:08:13,207 --> 01:08:15,541
Whose phrase of sorrow
conjures the wandering stars,

1635
01:08:15,541 --> 01:08:18,196
and makes them stand like
wonder-wounded hearers?

1636
01:08:18,196 --> 01:08:20,363
It is I, Hamlet, the Dane!

1637
01:08:21,378 --> 01:08:23,480
- The devil take thy soul!

1638
01:08:23,480 --> 01:08:25,575
- I prithee, take thy
fingers from my throat.

1639
01:08:25,575 --> 01:08:26,803
Hold off thy hand.

1640
01:08:26,803 --> 01:08:29,120
- Pluck them asunder.

1641
01:08:29,120 --> 01:08:31,449
- My lords, be quiet.

1642
01:08:31,449 --> 01:08:32,420
- [Servo] This must be an Irish funeral,

1643
01:08:32,420 --> 01:08:34,466
they're both drunk and fighting.

1644
01:08:34,466 --> 01:08:37,707
- Why, I will fight
with him upon this theme

1645
01:08:37,707 --> 01:08:40,638
until my eyelids will no longer wag!

1646
01:08:40,638 --> 01:08:41,971
I loved Ophelia!

1647
01:08:42,861 --> 01:08:44,049
- [Servo] We went steady.

1648
01:08:44,049 --> 01:08:46,233
- 40,000 brothers could not with all their

1649
01:08:46,233 --> 01:08:49,162
quantity of love make up my sum!

1650
01:08:49,162 --> 01:08:50,995
- [Crow] 50,000 maybe.

1651
01:08:52,644 --> 01:08:54,401
- What would thou do for her?

1652
01:08:54,401 --> 01:08:55,988
Swounds, show me what thou’lt do.

1653
01:08:55,988 --> 01:08:58,135
- [Servo] I'm trying to be dead in here.

1654
01:08:58,135 --> 01:08:59,400
- Would weep?

1655
01:08:59,400 --> 01:09:00,233
Would fight?

1656
01:09:00,233 --> 01:09:01,066
Would fast?

1657
01:09:01,066 --> 01:09:01,899
Would tear thyself?

1658
01:09:01,899 --> 01:09:02,732
Would drink up vinegar, eat a crocodile?

1659
01:09:02,732 --> 01:09:03,565
I’ll do’t!

1660
01:09:03,565 --> 01:09:04,924
Dost thou come here to
whine, to outface me

1661
01:09:04,924 --> 01:09:06,657
with leaping into her grave?

1662
01:09:06,657 --> 01:09:07,757
- [Servo] He's getting German-er.

1663
01:09:07,757 --> 01:09:10,134
- Be buried alive with her, and so will I,

1664
01:09:10,134 --> 01:09:12,384
I’ll rant as well as thou.

1665
01:09:12,384 --> 01:09:14,839
- This is mere madness, oh my sons.

1666
01:09:14,839 --> 01:09:16,533
- [Crow] Loser tease.

1667
01:09:16,533 --> 01:09:17,564
- [Servo] Craplet.

1668
01:09:17,564 --> 01:09:22,397
- You sir, what is the
reason that you use me thus?

1669
01:09:22,397 --> 01:09:23,756
I love you, ever.

1670
01:09:23,756 --> 01:09:26,616
- [Servo] Okay was it her or me?

1671
01:09:26,616 --> 01:09:29,616
- It is no matter, the cat will mew,

1672
01:09:30,562 --> 01:09:32,467
and dog will have his day.

1673
01:09:32,467 --> 01:09:36,634
- [Crow] Pomeranian day,
Dotson day, Lhasa Otso day?

1674
01:09:39,151 --> 01:09:40,359
- [Servo] Wait, wait, I'm
supposed to be in front

1675
01:09:40,359 --> 01:09:41,692
of you, hold up.

1676
01:09:46,159 --> 01:09:51,030
- [Mike] Hey, Laertes, lean
on the headstones, fun.

1677
01:09:51,030 --> 01:09:52,981
- Will you be ruled, my lord?

1678
01:09:52,981 --> 01:09:54,146
- [Crow] Well I've got an attractive offer

1679
01:09:54,146 --> 01:09:56,313
from the king of Flanders.

1680
01:09:57,221 --> 01:09:59,005
- Might I offer it to you.

1681
01:09:59,005 --> 01:10:00,877
So you may not overrule me to to a peace.

1682
01:10:00,877 --> 01:10:02,044
- Would I not?

1683
01:10:03,065 --> 01:10:06,607
- [Servo] Listen, I've
got some cuties here.

1684
01:10:06,607 --> 01:10:08,931
- I will work him to an exploit,

1685
01:10:08,931 --> 01:10:12,266
new-ripe in my devising,
under the which he shall

1686
01:10:12,266 --> 01:10:14,092
not choose but fall!

1687
01:10:14,092 --> 01:10:16,709
And for his death no wind
of blame shall breathe,

1688
01:10:16,709 --> 01:10:19,554
but even his mother shall
uncharge the practice,

1689
01:10:19,554 --> 01:10:21,304
and call it accident!

1690
01:10:22,288 --> 01:10:23,528
- My lord, I shall be ruled.

1691
01:10:23,528 --> 01:10:24,961
- [Crow] Wide ruled or college ruled?

1692
01:10:24,961 --> 01:10:28,341
- And the better if you could devise it so

1693
01:10:28,341 --> 01:10:29,854
that I might be the organ.

1694
01:10:29,854 --> 01:10:31,955
- It falls right.

1695
01:10:31,955 --> 01:10:33,419
What would you undertake to show yourself

1696
01:10:33,419 --> 01:10:37,100
in deed your father's son more than words?

1697
01:10:37,100 --> 01:10:38,382
- Cut his throat in the church.

1698
01:10:38,382 --> 01:10:40,241
- [Servo] Now see that's
a little over the top.

1699
01:10:40,241 --> 01:10:44,059
- No place, indeed,
should murder sanctuarize,

1700
01:10:44,059 --> 01:10:46,559
revenge should have no bounds!

1701
01:10:47,490 --> 01:10:50,346
But, good Laertes, we’ll
set on those who shall

1702
01:10:50,346 --> 01:10:51,685
praise your excellence.

1703
01:10:51,685 --> 01:10:53,526
- [Servo] What about my church idea?

1704
01:10:53,526 --> 01:10:55,385
- And put a double varnish on the fame

1705
01:10:55,385 --> 01:10:58,769
the Frenchman gave you, in fine together,

1706
01:10:58,769 --> 01:11:01,426
and bring you, and wager on your heads!

1707
01:11:01,426 --> 01:11:04,343
He, being free from all contriving,

1708
01:11:05,619 --> 01:11:07,803
will not peruse the foils, and remiss,

1709
01:11:07,803 --> 01:11:10,053
or with a little shuffling,

1710
01:11:11,164 --> 01:11:13,208
you may choose a sword unabated.

1711
01:11:13,208 --> 01:11:17,375
And in a pass of practice,
requite him for your father!

1712
01:11:19,040 --> 01:11:20,020
- I will do it.

1713
01:11:20,020 --> 01:11:22,545
- [Crow] I will cut his
throat in the church.

1714
01:11:22,545 --> 01:11:24,709
- And for that purpose
I’ll anoint my sword.

1715
01:11:24,709 --> 01:11:26,534
- [Servo] Well that's up to you.

1716
01:11:26,534 --> 01:11:29,221
- I bought an unction from a mountebank.

1717
01:11:29,221 --> 01:11:33,388
I'll touch the point with
his contagion, so that--

1718
01:11:34,605 --> 01:11:36,173
- [Servo] Yes, yes, go on.

1719
01:11:36,173 --> 01:11:38,094
- [Crow] And cut his throat in the church.

1720
01:11:38,094 --> 01:11:39,777
- [Servo] No.

1721
01:11:39,777 --> 01:11:41,444
- If it should fail?

1722
01:11:47,968 --> 01:11:48,801
I have it.

1723
01:11:48,801 --> 01:11:51,968
- [Crow] Cut his throat in the church.

1724
01:11:52,923 --> 01:11:54,585
- When in your motion you are hot and dry

1725
01:11:54,585 --> 01:11:57,607
and make your bouts more
violent to that end,

1726
01:11:57,607 --> 01:12:00,961
so that he calls for drink,
I’ll have prepared him

